  "id": "measurement-level",
  "term": "measurement level",
  "definition": "Measurement level is the broad type of method used to assess a psychological response or process. In this source, it refers to whether emotions are measured through physiological signals, behavioral responses, or cognitive self-report methods such as ratings and questionnaires.",
